const content="<article data-editorial-version=\"3\" class=\"sn-page\"><div class=\"sn-read\"><a href=\"/supporters/\">← Featured sponsors</a><p class=\"sn-kicker\">Marine Diesel Engine · Sponsor feature</p><img class=\"sn-logo\" src=\"/images/supporters/survival-official-logo.png\" alt=\"SURVIVAL First Aid Kits logo\" width=\"210\" height=\"100\"><h1>SURVIVAL: first-aid kits for the people working and sailing aboard</h1><p class=\"sn-intro\">SURVIVAL supplies marine first-aid kits that keep dressings, bandages and other items organised together. Whether the day involves boat maintenance or a trip with friends, a kit gives first-aid equipment a known place aboard.</p><img class=\"sn-hero\" src=\"/images/supporters/ocean-warrior.jpg\" alt=\"SURVIVAL Ocean Warrior kit and waterproof dry bag\" width=\"900\" height=\"900\"><section><h2>Keep supplies as organised as your tools</h2><p>Owners often know where their spare parts and tools are kept. First-aid supplies should be just as recognisable to the people using the boat. SURVIVAL offers complete kits and replacement items to keep them stocked after use.</p><p>We like that ongoing practicality. A kit should remain useful from one visit to the next, rather than slowly losing contents that nobody replaces. Organisation helps an owner see what they carry and gives the crew something clear to retrieve.</p></section><section><h2>Storage options for boating</h2><p>Ocean Warrior is a compact kit developed with Mark Visser. It floats and comes with a waterproof dry bag. The Marine Scale G kit uses a waterproof box, providing another format for protecting supplies aboard.</p><p>These choices let owners consider where the kit will live and whether it needs to travel between boats or activities. We appreciate that the storage format is treated as part of the equipment&#x27;s usefulness.</p></section><section><h2>Why we feature SURVIVAL</h2><p>The Australian brand dates to 1988, but our reason for featuring it is its practical product offering. First-aid supplies are for people, and they need to be where those people work and spend time.</p><p>For readers who maintain their own vessels, a complete kit belongs alongside the equipment that keeps the boat ready. Suitable storage and the ability to restock make it a straightforward part of preparing for both work aboard and leisure afloat.</p></section><div class=\"sn-contact\"><a href=\"https://survivalfirstaidkits.net.au/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"sponsored nofollow noopener noreferrer\">Explore SURVIVAL first-aid kits ↗</a><a href=\"/supporters/\">More featured sponsors</a></div></div></article><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"Article\", \"headline\": \"SURVIVAL: first-aid kits for the people working and sailing aboard\", \"description\": \"SURVIVAL supplies marine first-aid kits that keep dressings, bandages and other items organised together.\", \"image\": \"https://marinedieselengine.com.au/images/supporters/ocean-warrior.jpg\", \"author\": {\"@type\": \"Organization\", \"name\": \"Marine Diesel Engine\"}, \"dateModified\": \"2026-11-05\", \"mainEntityOfPage\": \"https://marinedieselengine.com.au/supporters/survival-kit/\"}</script>";
